WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.336 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:08.174
-Larva is singular.
Larvae is plural.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:12.111
The actor in "Goliath Awaits"
is named Robert Forster,

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:13.546
not Robert Forrester.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.414
Shame on me.
He's a wonderful actor.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:17.016
"Jackie Brown?"

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.918
[ Silence ]

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.686
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.855
We said we were going
to keep showing clips

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.390
from "Goliath Awaits,"

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.460
but we did not have
permission last week

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.897
and now we're in a bit
of a legal tangle

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:34.433
with Larry White Productions.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:38.270
This is fascinating -- I saw
this on the Wikipedia page.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.107
The original "Goliath Awaits"
is 200 minutes,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:45.244
but if you get it on VHS,
it's only 110 minutes.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.845
And I think it says a lot
about the script

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:49.315
that you can cut out
90 minutes

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.551
and maintain the integrity
of the story.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:54.186
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.222
I guess it was originally
110 minutes,

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.192
but in order to make
it a two-night...

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:03.596
miniseries event, they needed
to get it up to 200 minutes.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.400
And if you're wondering how
they took 110 minutes script

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.301
and got to 200 minutes,

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.070
they had Reese do a pass.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.107
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:20.946
Now, Seth Reese,
that's our writer.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.816
and again, that was a burn.
Not particularly a fair one.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.985
But in return for the burn,
I'm going to remind you

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.655
he's got a new film
coming out called "The Menu."

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.290
This is a --
This is not me joking around.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.623
This is a "Vanity Fair"
headline --

00:01:31.623 --> 00:01:33.526
"'The Menu' is not what
you expect -- it's better."

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.529
So keep an eye out
for "The Menu,"

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.665
and you'll continue, obviously,
to see us plugging it here

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:42.668
because we are going to
continue to burn Reese

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:44.270
and feel bad about it.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.607
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:50.476
Oh, I said clouds were made
from "da air,"

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:53.413
when in fact, they're made from
water droplets or ice crystals.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.849
In my defense, I did say
they were made from "da air"

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.451
from the perspective
of Mike Lindell,

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.120
as evidenced by the fact that
instead of saying "the air,"

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.456
"da air."

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.524
And I feel like
when I'm in character

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.460
that you cannot correct that,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.095
when I'm in the middle
of one of my impressions,

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.529
because that's not me anymore.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.432
That's someone
speaking through me.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:16.002
That's why the impressions
are so good.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.672
I'm channeling them,
and it feels seamless

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.040
when you watch A Closer Look

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.875
and you see me doing
someone like Mike Lindell,

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:24.677
but we have to make edits

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.479
because obviously,
for people in the studio,

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.080
they know that before I do
a Mike Lindell,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.315
it's like... [ Gurgles ]

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.018
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.119
It's pretty long.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.821
It's like an incantation
and a pretty --

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.858
it's not fun to be here live.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:42.261
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.464
We mentioned a cheese ball tub
full of Xanax

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.199
and we showed a graphic,
and according to many of you,

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:50.570
the pills in the tub were
the wrong shape to be Xanax.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.970
So for everyone
who pointed that out,

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.941
I know this goes without saying,
but you gotta to relax.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.977
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.083
Costco doesn't sell giant tubs
of cheese ball.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.985
This is actually --
I'm reading this verbatim.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.453
This is something
that was said in --

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.488
"Costco doesn't sell
giant tubs of cheese balls.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.457
Do you even have
a Costco membership?"

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.026
I do not.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.995
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.097
Not only do I not buy
my cheese balls in bulk,

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:21.234
I buy them one at a time.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.135
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.406
Go to my artisanal
cheese ball guy.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.708
"Just one, Pierre -- Brie."

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.244
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.947
But nobody in Manhattan
shops at Costco.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:36.349
That's the reality of it.
Nobody has space.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.485
Should we buy bulk cheese balls
or have a sink?

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.188
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.188
[ Clears throat ]

00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:44.423
I said "mashinations."

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.492
I was told it was
"machinations."

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.027
I do know it's "machinations,"

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.463
but I avoid saying
"mack" just in general

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.799
because it reminds me
of you know who --

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:59.238
this -- this monster.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.273
This -- Who's scarier?

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:02.708
Really, just real quick.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:03.943
Who do you think is scarier,
"Black Phone" dude

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.445
or Mack the Knife?

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.180
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.819
♪ If you like burgers,
get in my van, kids ♪

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.855
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.992
I called the new break off
golf league

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.528
that's competing with the PGA,
I called it L-I-V.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.296
I guess it's "LIV."

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:25.898
And so I apologize.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.935
The last thing
I ever want to do

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:33.640
is offend a Saudi-backed
golf league.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.574
My apologies to the Saudi
royal family,

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.944
especially M-B-S.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:39.812
Sorry, MBS.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.216
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.616
I talked about
"The Little Mermaid."

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:47.653
I said Aree-elle
instead of Ari-el.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:49.188
I can explain.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.957
I have a sister in law
whose name is Ariel,

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:53.359
and when I first met her,

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:56.629
I accidentally said Ariel
and she slapped me in the face.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:05:00.700
So now I'm gun shy
to say Ariel.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.068
I just -- When I know --
Even when I know it's Ariel,

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:04.637
I say Ariel.
And it's funny, there,

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:08.408
about accidentally calling
my sister in law Ariel

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.743
because she's more of an Ursula.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.144
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:14.980
♪ This is why it's great
that no one in my family ♪

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.416
♪ Watches Corrections ♪

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:20.486
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.690
♪ They don't even know
it's a thing ♪

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.827
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.230
"Why do you get home
late on Thursdays now?"

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.233
♪ I'll never tell ♪

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.034
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:37.236
Hey, so, in Jokes I Can't Tell,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.071
we said that some
"Lord of the Rings" fans

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:41.407
are expressing anger
about Black hobbits.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.809
And a lot of
"Lord of the Rings" fans said,

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:46.245
"Hey, that's very unfair
to say that.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:48.180
You should have said
some bigots.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.883
Like, it's very unfair to,
you know, lump all of us

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.485
'Lord of the Rings'
fans together."

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.586
And that's very --
that's a very fair criticism.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:58.124
And I do want to apologize.
You know, I think the only thing

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:00.492
that it's safe to say about
all "Lord of the Rings" fans,

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:02.061
because, of course,
they contain multitudes --

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.763
the only thing
that's true of all of you

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.465
is you're incapable
of being bored.

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.768
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:15.207
We always end
Jokes Seth Can't Tell

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:17.142
by saying Black women
and lesbians are liars,

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:19.111
and when one of you said,
"What about Black lesbians?"

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.914
It's weird.
They're very honest.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.117
It's like a double negative
situation.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.854
Wanda Sykes tells you something?
Take it to the grave.

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:33.158
Hey, it's - it's Twinings,
not Twinnings.

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:35.995
I just genuinely didn't know
that, but I messed that up.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:40.800
Also, the Queen drank
Gordon's gin, not Beefeater.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.401
Vegan.

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:45.238
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.638 --> 00:06:47.806
Where...

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:50.542
[ Laughs, clears throat ]

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:53.245
Oh, this is cool.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:56.882
You guys, Detroit style pizza
is back at Pizza Hut,

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:59.852
third year in a row
that they brought it back.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:01.587
Their rectangular-shaped pie
with a thick,

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.156
crispy crust edge comes loaded
with your choice of toppings

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.558
and premium
vine-ripened tomato sauce.

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:10.696
And, you know, I said it before.
I'll say it again.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.298
No one out-pizzas the Hut.

00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:16.969
And that's just --
this is something I believe.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.971
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.474
Okay?

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:24.043
This is me sharing some --
It's not even a correction.

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:27.479
I mean, the correction
was Detroit style pizza was gone

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:30.483
and now it's back again.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:34.587
Because again, if that was -- if
that was a paid consideration

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:35.788
furnished by Pizza Hut,

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:38.924
we legally would have to put it
on a chyron

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:40.526
that we'd keep up for, like,
two and a half seconds.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.931 line:0%
I'm not just allowed to say it.

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:51.103
I will say,
it would be pretty cool

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:53.205
if a brand decided
to pay some money

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:55.508
to get their name
in Corrections.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:58.677
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:02.881
If I was a jackal, trying to
decide between two pizza places,

00:08:02.881 --> 00:08:04.784
that might tip the scales.

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.719
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:10.356
Pretty cool.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:13.125
Maybe a wake-up call
for other brands out there.

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.627
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.728 --> 00:08:18.364
Get a bidding war going.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.836
Hey, sometimes I got
to give jackals credit

00:08:24.836 --> 00:08:28.140
where credit is due -- I talked
about Jacques Cousteau's

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.346
short-lived 1960s
[French accent] Canal+

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:36.915
[normally] prank show "Jaque'd."

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:39.385
The only downside is
more than one of you

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:41.387
had a better one,
and to be honest,

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:42.989
I'm more impressed
when it's just one person.

00:08:42.989 --> 00:08:44.623
But this would have been better.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:46.425 line:0%
Congratulations, jackals.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.195 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.665
Oh, there was such a --
it was all sort

00:08:53.665 --> 00:08:57.135
of sea life-style pranks.

00:08:57.135 --> 00:08:59.705
And there was a really
good episode where

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:03.442
their Steve-O,
Etienne Oh.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.578
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.578 --> 00:09:08.079
It was called the sperm whale,

00:09:08.079 --> 00:09:10.216
and it wasn't the mammal.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:11.951
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.855
We mentioned the Cake song --

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:17.823
the band Cake's song
"Going the Distance,"

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:19.791
you know, which obviously,
I don't have to tell you

00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:21.060
is on the album
"Fashion Nugget."

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.228
But then when we put up the key,

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:25.564
the key was the album
"Prolonging the Magic."

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.600
And I was obviously as surprised
as anybody else

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.201
in A Closer Look,
and you could feel the gasp

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.502
from the audience
because everybody,

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:32.237
I think, both was on board
with the Cake reference

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:35.107
and very surprised
that we put up the wrong album.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:38.610
And and so I went --
I went down to Graphics

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.013
and wanted to unload on them,
but they weren't the problem.

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.516
The problem was
one of our producers,

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:46.852
Emily Erotas, is a huge --
just a huge Cake fan.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:48.320
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.022
She's a Cake head.

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:53.125
A great producer --
fast, thorough, sharp as a tack,

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:55.193
but she's always felt
very strongly

00:09:55.193 --> 00:09:59.064
that "Prolonging the Magic"
is THE Cake album.

00:09:59.064 --> 00:10:01.834
And so I guess she overruled
the graphics department,

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.736
and I just went, "Ugh."

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:06.138
I mean, I marched into
her office and I'm like,

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:07.506
"Do you really think
'Prolonging the Magic'

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:08.707
is better than
'Fashion Nugget?'"

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:09.708
And she was like, "Yes, I do."
And I'm like,

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:12.244
"Even after Damiani
and Brown left?"

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:13.912
And she's like,
"Because they left."

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:15.448
And then you're just like,
enough.

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:17.416
[ Laughter ]

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:18.751
When you're arguing Cake
with Emily,

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:21.053
it's just sometimes
just better to walk away.

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:22.455
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.327
You can legally drive
a golf court --

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:30.363
a golf cart
on the highway in Florida

00:10:30.363 --> 00:10:32.764
as long as can reach a minimum
speed of 40 miles per hour.

00:10:32.764 --> 00:10:34.333
Someone told me this and said
if I didn't believe him,

00:10:34.333 --> 00:10:35.567
I could look it up

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:38.638
in the Florida statutes
for motor vehicles.

00:10:38.638 --> 00:10:41.873
So I looked up
the Florida statutes for,

00:10:41.873 --> 00:10:43.241
you know, motor vehicles

00:10:43.241 --> 00:10:45.710
and I decided I would just,
like, open Apple+F

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:48.681
old "golf carts" to go to,
you know, the one mention.

00:10:48.681 --> 00:10:50.215
Guess how many times
"golf carts"

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:54.520
is mentioned in the Florida
statutes for motor vehicles?

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.290
57 times.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.760
Tell me you're a legal document
from Florida without telling me

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.164
you're a legal document
from Florida.

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:08.767
Oh. So we were talking about --
I accidentally said The Fonzie,

00:11:08.767 --> 00:11:12.203
and then I explained it
by saying I was talking about

00:11:12.203 --> 00:11:13.472
the Russian "Happy Days,"

00:11:13.472 --> 00:11:14.907
which of course, we mentioned
is called...

00:11:19.044 --> 00:11:20.779
That was who
The Fonzie was from.

00:11:20.779 --> 00:11:22.113
But a lot of you said

00:11:22.113 --> 00:11:24.816
there is no word for "the"
in the Russian language.

00:11:24.816 --> 00:11:27.286
So the only way to distinguish
one Fonzie

00:11:27.286 --> 00:11:29.855
from the other Fonzies
in Russian

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:33.658
would be to call him
Only Fonzie.

00:11:33.658 --> 00:11:36.361
And I think that's better.

00:11:36.361 --> 00:11:38.663
If instead of the Fonz,
it was Only Fonz.

00:11:38.663 --> 00:11:40.199
[ Laughs ]

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:41.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.102
Heyyy, Only Fonz.

00:11:43.102 --> 00:11:44.670
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:49.508
And then, you know --
someone was -- you know --

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:52.278
And again, I --
Credit where credit is due,

00:11:52.278 --> 00:11:54.880
I thought maybe I should write
the full lyrics to

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.282
"These Days, While Not Happy,
are Still Days,"

00:11:57.282 --> 00:11:58.717
but one -- a jackal did,

00:11:58.717 --> 00:12:00.585
and I'd just like to read them
because I do actually think

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:02.354
it's a beautiful piece of work.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.189
And again, so this would be,
obviously --

00:12:04.189 --> 00:12:06.425
this would be a show
that came out, you know,

00:12:06.425 --> 00:12:09.061
based on --
the world we're setting up here

00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:11.997
would be on television in Russia
from like '74 to '84,

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.865
but it would be about Russia
in the '50s,

00:12:13.865 --> 00:12:16.401
just like our "Happy Days."
You follow, Shoemaker?

00:12:16.401 --> 00:12:17.536
Do you follow?

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:19.171
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:20.706
I wish you could see his face.
He's like...

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.449
All right. Here we go.

00:12:30.449 --> 00:12:32.484
[Russian accent] ♪ Sunday,
Monday, these are days ♪

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:34.519
♪ Tuesday, Wednesday,
also days ♪

00:12:34.519 --> 00:12:36.255
♪ Thursday, Friday, again,
are days ♪

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:38.157
♪ No weekends, work begins ♪

00:12:38.157 --> 00:12:40.292
♪ Stalin is great for you ♪

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:43.195
♪ These days are devoid of joy ♪

00:12:43.195 --> 00:12:44.630
♪ That's every day ♪

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.299
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:50.836
[Normally] Again, this is based
on the previous Russia.

00:12:50.836 --> 00:12:53.572
The not fun one.

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.641
[ Laughter ]

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:56.542
Well...

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:05.217
"The Menu," in theaters...

00:13:05.217 --> 00:13:06.819
What?

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:07.953
Not anymore?

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:10.990
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:16.829
All right, you guys.

00:13:16.829 --> 00:13:18.664
I'm very happy
to be with you again.

00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:21.233
Hey, why don't you see me
next week?

